        <item>
            <key> <string>description</string> </key>
            <value> <string encoding="cdata"><![CDATA[

Inspect one or more ERP5 modules to discover their searchable fields and schema.\n
\n
    Returns columns, searchable columns, sortable columns, allowed portal types,\n
    and default sort order for each module.\n
\n
    USE THIS WHEN:\n
    - You need to know what fields can be used in erp5_search queries or select_list.\n
    - You want to discover sortable columns before searching or collecting.\n
    - You need to find what portal types a module contains.\n
\n
    DO NOT USE THIS WHEN:\n
    - You need the full list of modules - use erp5_discover first.\n
    - You want to read a specific document\'s fields - use erp5_read instead.\n
\n
    TYPICAL FLOW: erp5_discover (get module IDs) -> erp5_inspect (learn fields)\n
    -> erp5_search (catalog) or erp5_collect (the module\'s own listbox).\n
    

]]></string> </value>
